SUMMARY:MADGEN Theatre Festival
DESCRIPTION:Theatre of the Beat’s MADGEN Theatre Festival is a 3-day new play festival located in Toronto’s East Danforth neighbourhood. This year’s program presents four Canadian plays: PEACHES by Elio Zarrillo; Uprooted by Kabrena Robinson; Problematic History Teacher by MJ Kang; and I Have a Dream in Chinese by Irene Yi – each exploring personhood through intimate narratives that centre personal identity in the Canadian context.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/madgen-theatre-festival/
LOCATION:Danforth Mennonite Church\, 2174 Danforth Ave.\, Toronto
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://d28bcn7yu97icd.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/23122237/5.jpeg
ORGANIZER;CN="Theatre of the Beat":MAILTO:johnny@theatreofthebeat.ca
END:VEVENT
